    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for offensive production today led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who anchors the lineup with a 74.75 efficiency score against Bassitt. Despite a slight platoon disadvantage, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a significant park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable batting order position, cementing his status as the highest-ceiling play on the roster. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** also project strongly against Corbin, with both leveraging a favorable park environment to maintain scores above 66.0. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a traditional dynamic platoon penalty, his elite spot at number two in the order keeps his output potential high, provided he can navigate the league-wide focus on stolen base efficiency against today\u2019s battery.\n\n**Sam Antonacci** and **Josh Jung** round out our core, both drawing favorable matchups against Woods Richardson and Arrighetti, respectively. **Sam Antonacci** receives a healthy 19% boost due to the opponent's xERA, and his leadoff role is critical for maximizing our chances in the Runs category. The most difficult personnel decision of the day involved **Miguel Vargas**; he finished with a respectable 60.20 score but was ultimately relegated to the bench. While his matchup against Woods Richardson is technically favorable, the optimizer prioritized the higher base projections and situational advantages offered by **Josh Jung** and our primary infielders. **Dominic Smith** remains on the bench as well, falling short of our efficiency floor due to an unfavorable lefty-on-lefty platoon dynamic against Tolle. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker**, who are currently unavailable, ensuring we optimize our limited games-played cap with the healthy options at hand.",
